<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A2206001003">
<title>
Toe Adjustment
</title>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
The rack boot may break if it is twisted.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Check that the rack boot does not get twisted during adjustment of front wheel alignment.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Never adjust only right or left tie-rod, adjust both tie-rods by the same amount.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Loosen tie-rod end lock nuts.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Tighten or loosen right and left tie-rods by the same amount to adjust toe to specification.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Check that length “a” on right tie-rod is equal to that on left tie-rod. If they are not equal, readjust toe.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A220002.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "41.814mm" ver = "01" gw = "199" gh = "102"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Tighten tie-rod end lock nuts to specified torque. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A6206020"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A2206001004">
<title>
Reference Information
</title>
<topic id = "AENLSB0A2206001005">
<title>
Side slip
</title>
<ptxt>
When checked using side slip tester, side slip should be within the following specification.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
The side slip is only applicable for regulation required countries.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<spec-sdm>
<sdm-title>
Side slip (On one person)
</sdm-title>
<sdm1>
<sdm-condition>
</sdm-condition>
<sdm-value>
OUT 5 to IN 5 mm/m (OUT 0.20 to IN 0.20 in./3.4 ft.)
</sdm-value>
</sdm1>
</spec-sdm>
<ptxt>
If side slip deviates from specification greatly, front wheel alignment may be out of specification.
</ptxt>
</topic>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A2206001007">
<title>
Camber, Caster and Kingpin Inclination Angle Inspection
</title>
<ptxt>
Check camber, caster and kingpin inclination angle using camber caster kingpin gauge (1) and turning radius gauge (2). If measured value is not as specified, check the following items for damage, deformation and crack. Repair or replace any defective part.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Strut assembly components
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Suspension arms and bushings
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Front suspension frame
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Front wheel hubs, steering knuckles and wheel bearings
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Vehicle body
</ptxt>
